<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48431" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tīthōnus</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-nos</span></b> , i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τιθωνός,</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>son of
			Laomedon</i>, <i>consort of Aurora</i>, <i>and father of Memnon; endowed with immortality</i>,
				<i>and changed at last</i>, <i>after
				reaching a decrepit old age</i>, <i>into a
			cicada</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Sen. 1, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 4,
				585</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. F. 6, 473</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 2,
				16, 30</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 28, 8</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tithoni conjux,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. H.
				17</span></i>
			 (18), 111.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tīthōnĭus</span></b> , a,
			um, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>belonging to Tithonus</i>, <i>Tithonian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conjux,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Aurora</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. F.
					3, 403</span></i>
			.—Called also, <i>absol.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tīthōnia</span></b> ,
				<i><span class="en">Ov. F.
				4, 943</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Val. Fl. 1, 311</span></i>; <i><span class="en">3, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Stat. Th. 12,
				3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">senectus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					S. 4, 3, 151</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tīthōnaeus</span></b> ,
				a, um, adj., <i>of</i>
			or <i>belonging to Tithonus</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Memnon,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Avien. Perieg. 368</span></i>
			. — </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Tīthōnis</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., <i>the wife of Tithonus</i>, i. e. <i>Aurora</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Stat.
				S. 5, 1, 34</span></i>.</div>
